On 7/19/2015 4:10 AM, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> We need all of these to be in jbovlaste for the glossary generation.
>
> If any of them are flat-out invalid, let me know and I'll mark them
> as such in the source.

A high percentage of those come from the lujvo-making examples, and it 
doesn't really make sense to define them in jbovlaste.  They are not 
"flat-out-invalid" but rather are allowed but dispreferred forms.  The 
scoring algorithm tells which are less-preferred, and I'm pretty sure 
the text makes it evident as well, so I'm not sure that any special 
marking is needed.

In the following, only one cmene and one lujvo in the first bunch are 
used (lojbangirz being the name-form that has been used the longest), 
and all of the second bunch are equivalent to the shortest one.

If people insist on putting a definition in jbovlaste, a "see [preferred 
form]" would be the best approach, ISTM

